WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is very exciting.
I love this.

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
You and Nick have
written a book together.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:04.437 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Greatest Love Story --"
What is it?

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:07.240
"Greatest Love Story Ever Told."
-"Ever Told," Seth. Ever.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.577
-And, now, I know Nick
has written books before.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But this is your first time
writing one with him.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:14.514 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Was this his idea?

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whose idea was it
to write one together?

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was completely my idea.
-Okay.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:21.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I had to talk him into it,
twist his arm.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, finally,
he was really into it.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.791 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So, what we did was --

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were on the road
with my band, actually.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, we were just in
various hotels

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.463 line:92%
and we'd be laying in bed.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:34.701
He's not normally allowed to
speak to me when we're in bed.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:38.104 line:92%
Touching only, no speaking.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.674 size:84% position:42%
But I made an exception
and I said, "Hey --"

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.610 size:78% position:39%
'Cause we already had
our chapter ideas.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Hey, why don't we
knock out a chapter."

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.180 line:92%
So he pulled out his phone,

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.114 line:92%
turned on the tape recorder,

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.417 size:88% position:44%
and then we just start
talking about, you know,

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:55.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
families or religion or
whatever the chapter was about

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:57.257 line:92%
and whatever the topic was.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then that's what
the book is.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's kind of, like,
interview-magazine style.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just us having
real conversations.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
-It's so cool. It's fun.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:09.002
-One thing we have in common,
which I always forget, is --

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
we both went to
Northwestern University.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know. I can't believe that.
I always forget that.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you did not stay
till the end.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.177 line:92%
-No. I'm a college dropout.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're a college dropout,
but the story --

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You said that very politely.
-Yes.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:25.151
Well, because it wasn't
like you didn't have the grades.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had something better
than college.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:33.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was doing -- I got a show
downtown that went pro.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, I went back for
my junior year,

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was having
a hard time doing

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:38.498 line:92%
eight shows a week downtown

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:41.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
and doing, you know,
like, a full load of classes.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:41.601 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I went in to talk to
the dean, to get her advice,

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:48.208 line:92%
and she was like, "Drop out."

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "That is not
what I was expecting.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.980
And she said, "Well, you're
doing what you want to do,

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.248 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
so who cares?"

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
-Yeah.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That really speaks to
the school that they realized,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We don't have anything
else to teach you.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.490 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You're already there."

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you've certainly done
the school proud.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You too.
-Thank you very much.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.195
It's always so great to see you.
Thanks for being here, Megan.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.663 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

